{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For I have hardened.</b> Even though Moses said, יָדַעְתִּי כִּי טֶרֶם תִּירְאוּן (Exodus 9:30), he thought that even if Pharaoh would not submit to the blessed El out of fear of His greatness, he would at least listen once he was no longer able to endure the affliction of the plagues — and this is what Moses thought when, by the force of the plague, Pharaoh said, ה' הַצַּדִּיק (Exodus 9:27). However, when Moses saw that despite all this he did not listen, he thought that the warning had been in vain, for even when unable to endure he would not listen. Therefore the blessed HaShem said to him: even though now he too has hardened his heart, behold, I had already hardened his heart during the boils (Exodus 9:12) — and this was in order to multiply the signs in the midst of Egypt, so that some among them might return in repentance, and so that Israel might recount them to generations and recognize My greatness and My goodness. Therefore the warning is fitting even though Pharaoh will not listen." "<b>In order that I may set these signs of Mine in his midst.</b> So that through them the people may recognize My greatness and turn back from wickedness."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Resolved ה' to HaShem in the quoted phrase ה' הַצַּדִּיק from Exodus 9:27."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:02.579237248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}